00:49:04,310 --> 00:49:07,250
I was beginning to think[br]I was gonna have to go outside...

933
00:49:07,310 --> 00:49:10,580
and get one of[br]the goddamn maids to do it.

934
00:49:10,650 --> 00:49:12,590
Oh, no. I'll do it.

935
00:49:12,650 --> 00:49:14,810
Shit. What are friends for ?

936
00:49:14,890 --> 00:49:17,820
[ Groaning, Howling ]

937
00:49:17,890 --> 00:49:21,120
- ~ I think she'll know ~[br]- You ready ?

938
00:49:21,200 --> 00:49:24,100
- [ Groaning ][br]- ~ Where logic ~

939
00:49:24,160 --> 00:49:26,160
- Close your eyes.[br]- ~ And proportion ~

940
00:49:26,230 --> 00:49:28,260
- Yeah, good boy.[br]- [ Groaning Continues ]

941
00:49:28,340 --> 00:49:31,000
~ Have fallen[br]sloppy dead ~

942
00:49:31,070 --> 00:49:35,170
- Rabbit ! White Rabbit ![br]- Quiet, goddamn it ![br]You're wasting my time !

943
00:49:35,240 --> 00:49:38,700
[ Slurring ][br]Outta here, man ! Get outta here.

944
00:49:38,780 --> 00:49:40,710
~ [ Volume Increases ]

945
00:49:40,780 --> 00:49:45,620
- ~ Remember ~[br]- Okay, close those peepers. Ten...

946
00:49:45,690 --> 00:49:48,250
- [ Howling ][br]- ~ What the dormouse said ~

947
00:49:48,320 --> 00:49:51,550
- nine... hundred and eleven ![br]- ~ Feed your head ~

948
00:49:51,630 --> 00:49:53,560
Fifty-two !

949
00:49:53,630 --> 00:49:57,030
- ~ Feed your head ~[br]- Hey ! Hey !

950
00:49:57,100 --> 00:49:59,500
Hey ![br][ Shrieking ]

951
00:49:59,570 --> 00:50:01,260
[ Shouting ]

952
00:50:01,340 --> 00:50:03,830
[ Retching Loudly ]

953
00:50:03,900 --> 00:50:06,340
- [ Vomiting ][br]- I need sleep.

954
00:50:06,410 --> 00:50:08,340
[ Coughing ]

955
00:50:10,810 --> 00:50:13,250
[ Retching Continues ]

956
00:50:22,460 --> 00:50:24,360
[ Loud Roar ]

957
00:50:25,890 --> 00:50:28,920
Holy shit !

958
00:50:29,000 --> 00:50:31,860
Mace ! Mace, man.[br]You want this ?

959
00:50:34,770 --> 00:50:36,700
You'd do that,[br]wouldn't you?

960
00:50:36,770 --> 00:50:39,170
- Well, why not ?[br]- You fucking bastard !

961
00:50:39,240 --> 00:50:43,840
Hell, just a minute ago[br]you were asking me to kill you.[br]Now you wanna kill me.

962
00:50:43,910 --> 00:50:47,040
What I should do, goddamn it,[br]is call the fucking police !

963
00:50:47,110 --> 00:50:49,780
Boy, are you upset.

964
00:50:50,950 --> 00:50:53,610
There'd be no point, man,[br]calling the cops.

965
00:50:53,690 --> 00:50:55,620
There's no choice.

966
00:50:55,690 --> 00:50:59,630
I wouldn't dare go to sleep[br]with you wandering around[br]with a head full of acid...

967
00:50:59,690 --> 00:51:02,560
wanting to slice me up[br]with that goddamn knife.

968
00:51:02,630 --> 00:51:05,560
Who said anything[br]about slicing you up, man ?

969
00:51:07,970 --> 00:51:11,100
I just wanted to cut[br]a little "Z" in your forehead.

970
00:51:11,170 --> 00:51:13,160
[ Wheezing Laughter ]

971
00:51:13,240 --> 00:51:17,540
Get back in the tub.[br]Eat some reds and try to calm down.

972
00:51:17,610 --> 00:51:20,550
Smoke some grass.[br]Shoot some fucking smack.

973
00:51:20,610 --> 00:51:24,050
Shit, man, do whatever[br]you gotta do, but please...

974
00:51:24,120 --> 00:51:27,610
I need some fucking rest,[br]man. Please. Please.

975
00:51:27,690 --> 00:51:30,280
Get out of here,[br]you pig fucker !

976
00:51:30,360 --> 00:51:33,450
Up ! Up !

977
00:51:33,530 --> 00:51:36,460
Well, l, uh--

978
00:51:36,530 --> 00:51:38,460
Yeah.[br][ Panting ]

979
00:51:39,630 --> 00:51:42,260
You need to get to work.

980
00:51:42,340 --> 00:51:44,500
Goddamn, what a bummer.

981
00:51:44,570 --> 00:51:46,510
You scurvy[br]shyster bastard.

982
00:51:46,570 --> 00:51:49,300
- [ Groaning ][br]- I'm a Doctor of Journalism, man.

983
00:51:49,380 --> 00:51:51,310
Go on.

984
00:51:51,380 --> 00:51:53,470
- Don't let me keep you up.[br]- Now--

985
00:51:53,550 --> 00:51:56,780
Don't let me keep you up.[br][ Groans ]

986
00:51:56,850 --> 00:51:59,790
- [ Klaxon Blaring ][br]- Get in there and clean your shorts !

987
00:51:59,850 --> 00:52:02,720
Clean your shorts, goddamn it,[br]like a big boy !

988
00:52:02,790 --> 00:52:04,720
Pig !

989
00:52:07,590 --> 00:52:10,530
The acid had[br]shifted gears on him.

990
00:52:10,600 --> 00:52:14,530
The next phase would probably be[br]one of those hellishly intense[br]introspective nightmares.

991
00:52:14,600 --> 00:52:16,540
[ Mutters ][br]Must get some peace.

992
00:52:16,600 --> 00:52:19,830
- Four hours or so of catatonic despair.[br]- [ Gonzo Shouting ]

993
00:52:19,910 --> 00:52:23,000
- Damn drugs.[br]- Aaaaah !

994
00:52:23,440 --> 00:52:26,570
- Mmm ?[br]- [ Shouting Continues ]

995
00:52:29,120 --> 00:52:32,850
Ignore the nightmare[br]in the bathroom.

996
00:52:32,920 --> 00:52:36,180
Just another ugly refugee[br]from the love generation.

997
00:52:37,560 --> 00:52:40,460
My attorney had never been[br]able to accept the notion...

998
00:52:40,530 --> 00:52:42,960
often espoused[br]by former drug abusers...

999
00:52:43,030 --> 00:52:46,290
that you can get a lot higher[br]without drugs than with them.

1000
00:52:46,370 --> 00:52:48,300
Neither have l,[br]for that matter.

1001
00:52:48,370 --> 00:52:51,270
~ When the truth is found ~

1002
00:52:51,340 --> 00:52:55,740
~ To be lies ~

1003
00:52:55,810 --> 00:52:58,470
~ And all the joy ~

1004
00:52:58,550 --> 00:53:03,040
~ Within you dies ~

1005
00:53:03,120 --> 00:53:05,880
~ Don't you want[br]somebody to love ~

1006
00:53:05,950 --> 00:53:09,510
~ Don't you need[br]somebody to love ~

1007
00:53:09,590 --> 00:53:13,120
~ Wouldn't you love[br]somebody to love ~

1008
00:53:13,190 --> 00:53:18,220
~ You better find[br]somebody to love ~

1009
00:53:18,300 --> 00:53:20,290
~ Love ~

1010
00:53:20,370 --> 00:53:22,300
~ [ Continues ]

1011
00:53:22,370 --> 00:53:26,640
[ Duke Narrating ] 1965.[br]The great San Francisco acid wave.

1012
00:53:26,710 --> 00:53:28,870
~ When the garden flowers ~

1013
00:53:28,940 --> 00:53:33,880
I recall one night in a place[br]called the Matrix. There I was--

1014
00:53:33,950 --> 00:53:37,380
- ~ [ Continues ][br]- Mother of God. There I am.

1015
00:53:37,450 --> 00:53:39,390
Holy fuck.

1016
00:53:39,450 --> 00:53:43,750
Uh, clearly I was a victim[br]of the drug explosion...

1017
00:53:43,820 --> 00:53:47,560
a natural street freak[br]just eating whatever came by.

1018
00:53:47,630 --> 00:53:52,590
[ Voice Extremely Slowed Down ][br]Does anybody want some LSD ?

1019
00:53:52,670 --> 00:53:56,230
I got all the makin's...

1020
00:53:56,300 --> 00:53:59,000
right here !

1021
00:53:59,070 --> 00:54:04,910
[ Echoing ][br]All I need is a place to cook.

1022
00:54:07,980 --> 00:54:11,540
I decided to eat only[br]half of the acid at first...

1023
00:54:11,620 --> 00:54:15,420
but I spilled the rest on the sleeve[br]of my red woolen shirt.

1024
00:54:19,730 --> 00:54:23,790
[ Voice Slowed Down, Echoing ][br]What's the trouble ?

1025
00:54:23,860 --> 00:54:26,890
[ Voice Slowed Down, Echoing ][br]Well, all this white stuff...

1026
00:54:26,970 --> 00:54:30,060
on my sleeve...

1027
00:54:31,400 --> 00:54:35,500
is LSD.

1028
00:54:50,520 --> 00:54:52,220
[ Duke Narrating ][br]With a bit of luck...

1029
00:54:53,460 --> 00:54:55,190
his life[br]was ruined forever...

1030
00:54:55,260 --> 00:55:00,060
always thinking that just behind some[br]narrow door in all his favorite bars...

1031
00:55:00,130 --> 00:55:02,400
men in red woolen shirts...

1032
00:55:02,470 --> 00:55:06,410
are getting incredible kicks[br]from things he'll never know.

1033
00:55:09,180 --> 00:55:12,040
~ [ Pop: Mid-Tempo ]

1034
00:55:12,110 --> 00:55:15,810
Strange memories on[br]this nervous night in Las Vegas.

1035
00:55:15,880 --> 00:55:20,510
Has it been five years ? Six ?

1036
00:55:20,590 --> 00:55:25,720
It seems like a lifetime, the kind[br]of peak that never comes again.

1037
00:55:25,790 --> 00:55:28,820
~ Love is but[br]a song we're singin' ~

1038
00:55:28,900 --> 00:55:31,390
San Francisco[br]in the middle '60s...

1039
00:55:31,470 --> 00:55:35,400
was a very special time and place[br]to be a part of...

1040
00:55:35,470 --> 00:55:38,130
- but no explanation...[br]- ~ We can make the mountains ring ~

1041
00:55:38,210 --> 00:55:40,140
no mix of words[br]or music or memories...

1042
00:55:40,210 --> 00:55:43,700
can touch that sense of knowing[br]that you were there and alive...

1043
00:55:43,780 --> 00:55:47,740
in that corner of time in the world,[br]whatever it meant.

1044
00:55:47,820 --> 00:55:51,550
~ Though the bird[br]is on the wing ~

1045
00:55:51,620 --> 00:55:55,210
~ And you may not[br]know why ~

1046
00:55:57,120 --> 00:55:59,060
There was madness[br]in any direction...

1047
00:55:59,130 --> 00:56:01,420
- ~ Come on, people, now ~[br]- at any hour.

1048
00:56:01,500 --> 00:56:03,590
- ~ Smile on your brothers ~[br]- You could strike sparks anywhere.

1049
00:56:03,660 --> 00:56:06,060
~ Everybody get together ~

1050
00:56:06,130 --> 00:56:08,230
- ~ Try to love one another ~[br]- There was a fantastic[br]universal sense...

1051
00:56:08,300 --> 00:56:10,770
that whatever we were doing was right,[br]that we were winning.

1052
00:56:11,940 --> 00:56:14,240
And that, I think,[br]was the handle.

1053
00:56:14,310 --> 00:56:16,140
~ Some may come[br]and some may go ~

1054
00:56:16,210 --> 00:56:18,140
That sense[br]of inevitable victory...

1055
00:56:18,210 --> 00:56:19,770
over the forces[br]of old and evil.

1056
00:56:19,850 --> 00:56:23,080
Not in any mean or military sense--[br]we didn't need that.

1057
00:56:25,090 --> 00:56:27,780
Our energy[br]would simply prevail.

1058
00:56:27,860 --> 00:56:31,090
We had all the momentum.

1059
00:56:31,160 --> 00:56:34,650
We were riding the crest[br]of a high and beautiful wave.

1060
00:56:36,160 --> 00:56:41,000
- So now, less than five years later...[br]- ~ [ Continues ]

1061
00:56:41,070 --> 00:56:44,660
you can go up a steep hill[br]in Las Vegas and look west...

1062
00:56:44,740 --> 00:56:47,370
and with the right kind[br]of eyes...

1063
00:56:47,440 --> 00:56:50,500
you can almost see[br]the high-water mark...

1064
00:56:50,580 --> 00:56:53,510
that place where the wave[br]finally broke...

1065
00:56:53,580 --> 00:56:55,520
and rolled back.

1066
00:56:55,580 --> 00:56:59,520
- ~ Try to love one another right now ~[br]- [ Waves Gently Crashing ]

1067
00:57:01,920 --> 00:57:03,410
~ [ Electric Piano ]

1068
00:57:07,490 --> 00:57:09,930
~ [ Piano Continues,[br]Rock Band Begins ]

1069
00:57:10,000 --> 00:57:12,430
- [ Doorbell Buzzing ][br]- ~ Want some whiskey in your water ~

1070
00:57:12,500 --> 00:57:15,660
- Room service ![br]- ~ Some sugar in your tea ~

1071
00:57:15,740 --> 00:57:18,970
~ What's all these crazy questions[br]they're askin' me ~

1072
00:57:19,040 --> 00:57:21,970
- Good morning, sir.[br]- ~ This is the craziest party[br]there could ever be ~

1073
00:57:22,040 --> 00:57:24,980
What do you want, man ?[br]What do you want ?

1074
00:57:25,050 --> 00:57:26,980
- Room service.[br]- Get out.

1075
00:57:27,050 --> 00:57:29,980
- ~ Mama told me not to come ~[br]- You're in the wrong room.[br]Get the fuck out !

1076
00:57:30,050 --> 00:57:32,990
- I've got a gun. It's not mine, really.[br]- ~ Mama told me not to come ~

1077
00:57:33,050 --> 00:57:34,990
- Uh, the-- the-- the bill.[br]- What ?

1078
00:57:35,060 --> 00:57:37,990
- Will you... s-sign for it ?[br]- Yeah, I'll get it. Hurry up.

1079
00:57:38,060 --> 00:57:40,490
Don't move, man.[br]Be very still.

1080
00:57:40,560 --> 00:57:42,500
There we go.

1081
00:57:42,560 --> 00:57:44,500
Say nothing[br]to no one, man.

1082
00:57:44,570 --> 00:57:47,730
~ Open up the window[br]Let some air into this room ~

1083
00:57:47,800 --> 00:57:52,240
[ Duke Narrating ] The decision[br]to flee came suddenly. Or maybe not.

1084
00:57:52,310 --> 00:57:56,370
- ~ That cigarette you're smokin'[br]'bout scared me half to death ~[br]- Maybe I'd planned it all along,

1085
00:57:56,440 --> 00:57:58,810
subconsciously waiting[br]for the right moment.

1086
00:57:58,880 --> 00:58:01,750
- ~ Mama told me not to come ~[br]- The bill was a factor, I think...

1087
00:58:01,820 --> 00:58:04,610
- because I had no money to pay for it.[br]- ~ Mama told me not to come ~

1088
00:58:04,690 --> 00:58:08,620
Our room service tabs had been[br]running somewhere between[br]29 and 36 dollars per hour...

1089
00:58:08,690 --> 00:58:11,620
- ~ That ain't the way[br]to have fun, son ~[br]- for 48 consecutive hours.

1090
00:58:11,690 --> 00:58:13,630
- Incredible.[br]- ~ That ain't the way to have fun ~

1091
00:58:13,690 --> 00:58:15,630
How could it happen ?

1092
00:58:15,700 --> 00:58:20,070
But by the time I asked this question,[br]there was no one around to answer it.

1093
00:58:20,130 --> 00:58:23,260
That rotten attorney of mine,[br]Dr. Gonzo, was gone.

1094
00:58:23,340 --> 00:58:25,270
He must have sensed trouble.

1095
00:58:25,340 --> 00:58:27,170
Hmm ? Ohh.

1096
00:58:27,240 --> 00:58:29,070
A "Z" ?

1097
00:58:29,140 --> 00:58:31,200
Panic.

1098
00:58:31,510 --> 00:58:36,110
It crept up my spine like[br]first-rising vibes of an acid frenzy.

1099
00:58:36,180 --> 00:58:40,120
- [ Bell Dings ][br]- All these horrible realities[br]began to dawn on me.

1100
00:58:40,190 --> 00:58:42,920
[ Duke ][br]Oh, fuck.

1101
00:58:42,990 --> 00:58:44,920
Here I was...

1102
00:58:44,990 --> 00:58:48,050
alone in Las Vegas,[br]completely twisted on drugs.

1103
00:58:48,130 --> 00:58:51,430
No cash,[br]no story for the magazine...

1104
00:58:51,500 --> 00:58:56,940
and on top of everything else[br]I had a gigantic goddamn[br]hotel bill to deal with.

1105
00:58:59,370 --> 00:59:01,770
I didn't even know[br]who'd won the race.

1106
00:59:01,840 --> 00:59:03,780
- Maybe nobody.[br]- [ Arguing ]

1107
00:59:03,840 --> 00:59:06,780
How would Horatio Alger[br]have handled this situation ?

1108
00:59:07,950 --> 00:59:11,250
Stay calm.[br]Stay calm.

1109
00:59:11,320 --> 00:59:13,650
I'm a relatively[br]respectable citizen.

1110
00:59:13,720 --> 00:59:16,750
- Multiple felon, perhaps,[br]but certainly not dangerous.[br]- [ Whistles ]

1111
00:59:16,820 --> 00:59:19,260
- [ Engine Revs ][br]- Taxi !

1112
00:59:19,330 --> 00:59:23,850
Luckily I had taken the soap[br]and grapefruit and other luggage[br]out to the car earlier.

1113
00:59:23,930 --> 00:59:25,460
Now--

1114
00:59:25,530 --> 00:59:27,470
it was only a matter[br]of slipping the noose.

1115
00:59:27,530 --> 00:59:31,330
Hey ! Here, take this.[br]All right.

1116
00:59:31,410 --> 00:59:35,500
- Mr. Duke ! Mr. Duke ![br]- Oh, shit.

1117
00:59:35,580 --> 00:59:39,880
- We've been looking for you.[br]- The game was up. They had me.

1118
00:59:39,950 --> 00:59:43,250
Many fine books have been written[br]in prison, huh ?

1119
00:59:43,320 --> 00:59:45,510
- Sir ?[br]- What ?

1120
00:59:45,590 --> 00:59:47,680
Um, this telegram[br]came for you.

1121
00:59:47,760 --> 00:59:50,750
Actually, it's not for you.[br]It's for somebody named, uh, Thompson.

1122
00:59:50,820 --> 00:59:54,190
But it says, "Care of Raoul Duke."[br]Do you-- Do you--

1123
00:59:54,260 --> 00:59:57,250
- Does that mean anything ?[br]- Yes, yes, it means a lot. Thanks.

1124
00:59:57,330 --> 01:00:00,770
- Yeah, I checked the register[br]for this man Thompson.[br]- [ Engine Revs ]

1125
01:00:00,830 --> 01:00:03,390
We don't show him, but I figured[br]he might be part of your team.

1126
01:00:03,470 --> 01:00:05,500
-He is. Don't worry. I'll get it to him.[br]-Yeah.

1127
01:00:05,570 --> 01:00:08,200
Um, what confused us[br]was, uh...

1128
01:00:08,280 --> 01:00:12,710
Dr. Gonzo's signature[br]on the telegram from Los Angeles[br]when we knew he was right here.

1129
01:00:12,780 --> 01:00:14,910
Right.[br]You did the right thing.

1130
01:00:14,980 --> 01:00:18,320
Never try to understand a press message.[br]About half the time, we use codes.

1131
01:00:18,390 --> 01:00:20,680
Especially with Dr. Gonzo.[br]See ya.

1132
01:00:20,750 --> 01:00:24,620
- Um, tell me.[br]- [ Tires Screech ]

1133
01:00:24,690 --> 01:00:27,250
When will the doctor[br]be awake ?

1134
01:00:27,330 --> 01:00:31,320
- Awake ? What do you mean ?[br]- Well, um...

1135
01:00:31,400 --> 01:00:35,060
my manager, Mr. Heem,[br]would like to meet him.

1136
01:00:35,140 --> 01:00:37,630
It's nothing unusual, um--

1137
01:00:37,700 --> 01:00:41,730
Mr. Heem likes to meet[br]all of our large accounts...

1138
01:00:41,810 --> 01:00:44,070
put'em on a personal basis,[br]you know ?

1139
01:00:44,140 --> 01:00:46,340
Just a chat and a handshake.[br]You understand.

1140
01:00:46,410 --> 01:00:48,350
Of course,[br]but if I were you...

1141
01:00:48,420 --> 01:00:50,820
I would leave the doctor alone[br]until after he's eaten his breakfast...

1142
01:00:50,880 --> 01:00:52,820
because he's[br]a very crude man.

1143
01:00:52,890 --> 01:00:55,350
Jesus God !

1144
01:00:55,420 --> 01:00:57,910
- No ![br]- [ Tires Screech ]

1145
01:00:57,990 --> 01:01:02,760
But he will be available,[br]huh, maybe later this morning ?

1146
01:01:02,830 --> 01:01:06,860
Look, the telegram[br]is actually all scrambled.

1147
01:01:06,930 --> 01:01:09,900
It's actually from Thompson,[br]not to him.

1148
01:01:09,970 --> 01:01:13,630
All right ? Now, I've got to go.[br]I've gotta get to the race.

1149
01:01:13,710 --> 01:01:16,440
- B-But there's no hurry.[br]The race is over.[br]- Not for me.

1150
01:01:16,510 --> 01:01:19,670
Well, um--[br]Let's have lunch !

1151
01:01:19,750 --> 01:01:22,240
Righty-o, man.[br]Righty-o.

1152
01:01:22,580 --> 01:01:28,040
- ~ Now, the bricks[br]lay on Grand Street ~[br]- Jesus.

1153
01:01:28,120 --> 01:01:33,060
Bad waves of paranoia.[br]Madness. Fear and loathing.

1154
01:01:33,130 --> 01:01:36,030
Intolerable vibrations[br]in this place. Get out.

1155
01:01:36,100 --> 01:01:38,030
The weasels were closing in.

1156
01:01:38,100 --> 01:01:40,330
I could smell the ugly brutes.

1157
01:01:40,400 --> 01:01:42,330
Do me one last favor, Lord.

1158
01:01:42,400 --> 01:01:45,960
Just give me five more high-speed hours[br]before You bring the hammer down.

1159
01:01:46,040 --> 01:01:51,200
